{
  "$description": "Decisions behind the offline-state text (w-sync-status, w-send-status, w-storage-meter): which time style to show, how to split a byte count into a value and a unit, which attributes hold a count text and its plural forms, the queue progress and the hour cycle. Each platform formats the final words with its own locale formatter. Source of truth: src/components/offline-text.js; spec: docs/offline-states.md.",
  "$note": "Generated by scripts/fixtures-build.mjs. `{\"$date\":\"YYYY-MM-DDTHH:mm:ss\"}` denotes a local-time date. Reimplement each fn natively and assert args → expected.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "fn": "timeStyle",
      "args": [
        {
          "$date": "2026-11-11T08:12:00"
        },
        {
          "$date": "2026-11-11T10:00:00"
        }
      ],
      "expected": "clock"
    },
    {
      "fn": "timeStyle",
      "args": [
        {
          "$date": "2026-11-11T00:00:00"
        },
        {
          "$date": "2026-11-11T23:59:00"
        }
      ],
      "expected": "clock"
    },
    {
      "fn": "timeStyle",
      "args": [
        {
          "$date": "2026-11-10T23:59:00"
        },
        {
          "$date": "2026-11-11T00:01:00"
        }
      ],
      "expected": "weekday"
    },
    {
      "fn": "timeStyle",
      "args": [
        {
          "$date": "2026-11-05T08:12:00"
        },
        {
          "$date": "2026-11-11T10:00:00"
        }
      ],
      "expected": "weekday"
    },
    {
      "fn": "timeStyle",
      "args": [
